old=line('- **The one-month window.**');op(old,old+'\n- **Group-opinion protection.** If a DRV opinion under § 7a(4b) assumed self-employment and a later status or insurance proceeding finds employment for the same contractual relationship, § 7a(4c) starts compulsory insurance only on notification of that decision if the worker had the comparable illness and old-age cover required by § 7a(5) sentence 1 no. 2. The contract must have been concluded within two years after receipt of the opinion. Same relationships require the same type and circumstances of work and uniform contractual agreements under paragraph 4b. The individual route\'s one-month application and consent requirements do not apply to this alternative. Under current § 7a(7), paragraph 4c expires at the end of 30 June 2027.','R72')
old=line('- **If employment is found later**');op(old,'- **If employment is found later**, and neither the individual one-month protection nor the qualifying group-opinion protection applies, ordinary contribution liability reaches back to the start of the work. Late-payment surcharges can follow, subject to the actual § 24 rules: where a contribution notice operates retrospectively, no surcharge is levied to the extent the debtor credibly shows lack of knowledge of the payment duty without fault ([§ 24(1), (2) SGB IV](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/sgb_4/__24.html)). Refer before the client signs or at once when it comes up.','R72')
