old=line('- **Late statutory contributions:**');op(old,old+' For a retrospective contribution notice, § 24(2) excludes the surcharge to the extent the debtor credibly shows lack of knowledge of the payment duty without fault.','R72')
old=line('- Everyone resident must hold cover:');op(old,'- Residents within [§ 193(3) VVG](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/vvg_2008/__193.html) must maintain a private policy with an insurer authorised to operate in Germany, covering at least outpatient and inpatient treatment. The combined absolute and percentage deductibles for those treatments must be capped at EUR 5,000 per insured person and calendar year; for Beihilfe entitlement the cap follows the proportion not covered by Beihilfe. Apply the express statutory exceptions: statutory-insured or compulsorily insured persons; free medical care, Beihilfe or comparable entitlements within their scope; Asylum Seekers Benefits Act entitlement; and the specified ongoing SGB XII chapters 3, 4 and 7 or SGB IX part 2 benefit recipients whose benefit receipt began before 1 January 2009, including interruptions shorter than one month. This is not a private-policy duty for every resident outside GKV. A voluntary statutory member is compulsorily insured in social care insurance ([§ 20(3) SGB XI](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/sgb_11/__20.html)).','R73')
old=line('- **Prepayments:**');op(old,'- **Prepayments:** due within ten days after each month. With full prior-year duty, each is the current rate on one twelfth of last year\'s qualifying fees; if duty existed for only part of that year, divide those fees by the number of begun calendar months in which duty existed. Until 1 March, use the amount due for the preceding December. The first prepayment duty begins ten days after the end of the month up to which the levy first had to be accounted for. None is due if the monthly amount would not exceed EUR 40 ([§ 27(3), (4) KSVG](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/ksvg/__27.html)). The KSK can reduce prepayments on application if this year\'s fees will be much lower. For stipulated duty from July through December 2025 and EUR 12,000 qualifying fees, six begun duty months give the 2026 monthly reference EUR 12,000 / 6 × 4.9% = EUR 98, rather than EUR 49 under a full-year denominator; the preceding-December rule still applies until 1 March. A mid-July start still counts July.','R74')
old=line('- **Barred:**');op(old,'- **Concurrent-status gate:** the applicant must be neither compulsorily insured under §§ 25 or 26 SGB III nor insurance-free under §§ 27 or 28. Minor employment under § 27(2) does not exclude entry.\n'+old,'R75')
old=line('- **Deadline:** within three months of starting.');op(old,'- **Deadline:** within three months of starting. If entry was blocked solely by a prior compulsory-insurance status under §§ 25 or 26 or insurance-free status under §§ 27 or 28, apply within three months after that exclusion ends. Insurance begins when the actual paragraph 1 and 2 conditions are first met.\n- **Suspension:** later compulsory insurance under §§ 25 or 26 or insurance-free status under § 27 suspends this insurance; a § 27(2) minor job does not. Paragraph 4 does not list § 28 in this suspension clause; the separate end-of-cover rules remain.','R75')
old='Register by the end of May 2026.';op(old,'Register within three months: the nominal end of May is Sunday 31 May 2026, so the ordinary deadline is Monday 1 June 2026 under [§ 26(3) SGB X](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/sgb_10/__26.html). This assumes no authority notice expressly fixing the day under that provision or authority-set appointment under § 26(5).','R76')
old=line('- **Arrears:** after two months');op(old,'- **Arrears:** after two months\' arrears the KSK sends a reminder warning of suspension. If more than one month\'s share remains unpaid two weeks after receipt, the KSK must issue a suspension decision; suspension starts three days after receipt of that decision, not automatically when the two weeks expire. It ends when all arrears and the health and care shares falling due during suspension are paid. The KSK can end it early on an instalment agreement (§ 16(2), applied correspondingly by § 16a(2) KSVG).','R77')
